BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:73cb25200b33e1394fbe41f80d36c090
DTSTAMP:20260920T025617Z
DTSTART:20261001T233000Z
DTEND:20261002T003000Z
SUMMARY:The Christ Church Cathedral Choir
DESCRIPTION:The Christ Church Cathedral Choir celebrates its 500th annive
 rsary with a program that showcases the rich musical legacy of a unique 
 foundation — one that is both Oxford’s cathedral and a college of th
 e University of Oxford. The program traces that history from John Tavern
 er\, appointed by Cardinal Wolsey in 1526 as the first Informator Choris
 tarum\, to more recently associated composers. A newly commissioned cant
 ata by Composer in Residence Nico Muhly explores how poetry\, art\, and 
 glass act as a membrane between the visible world and the divine. Direct
 or of Music\, Peter Holder\, directs and conducts the choir\, and overse
 es the musical development of the choristers\, organ scholars\, and acad
 emic clerks. Previously he held the post of Sub-Organist of Westminster 
 Abbey and was organist for the State Funeral of Her Late Majesty Queen E
 lizabeth II and the Coronation of Their Majesties King Charl\nhttps://ch
 apel.princeton.edu/events/christ-church-cathedral-choir
URL:https://chapel.princeton.edu/events/christ-church-cathedral-choir
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
